<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="067" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Copy the filing parent's mapped values whatever the caller can read on its columns; Repair copies field-secured values too (owner 2026-11-27)</title>
    <phase>6 W6 Standard, guards, docs, retirement</phase>
    <gate>UAC-r2 diff review against conditions C1–C7 (below) before merge</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes a field-security rule on the BFF create, send, push and Repair paths; security; bff-api.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Lifts a field-security mask on four write paths; every other boundary must hold exactly.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W6</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>065</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, field-mapping, security, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement the owner's decisions of 2026-11-27 (notes/decisions.md): (1) "Yes also field secured values": the Repair pass copies a value from a field-secured source column of the row's filing parent; (2) "a field to field copy executed regardless of the user as access to the destination record": a mapped value from the row's filing parent is read app-only and copied whatever the caller can read on that parent's COLUMNS. Within UAC-r2's conditions C1–C7.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE BFF developer; Dataverse write path; authorization.</role>
  <goal>From the row's own filing parent, a mapped source column is copied on create, email send, push and Repair whether or not it is field-secured and whether or not the caller can read it, except the closed deny-list of access-model columns (C3). The caller must still be able to read the parent RECORD (C1). Any other source keeps today's mask and field-secured drop.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 065 lifted `FieldSecuredSourceRule.Split` for the filing parent on create (table and id) and on push (listed Filing edge), but kept the read as the caller: `MappingSourceCallerMask` (#2188) on create and at email send (`SendTimeFieldMapping`), and `RetrieveSourceRecordValuesAsCallerAsync` on push. Repair (system principal) still never copies a field-secured source column (`RecordCreationService.Repair.cs` ~1370–1400). The owner now lifts the caller read for the filing parent and asks Repair to copy too. Consequence, owner-accepted: a caller who cannot read a secured parent column sees its value in the child's target column unless that target is secured too.
    </background>
    <uac-r2-conditions>
      C1. The FR-04 source Read probe stays AS THE CALLER and is REQUIRED. The app-only read lifts FIELD security only. If the caller cannot read the parent record, nothing is read app-only and nothing is copied, and the answer is the same as for an unknown id. Must-fire on create, send and push: caller without Read on the parent → no app-only read of the mapped columns happens and nothing is copied.
      C2. Filing parent only, decided by table AND id exactly as in 065. Push: listed Filing edges only (`IsListedFilingEdgeColumn` / family mode), decided before the source read. Send: only when the mapping source is the filing parent. Every other source keeps the mask and the Split drop. Must-fire for each surface.
      C3. A closed DENY-LIST of access-model columns never read past the mask, whatever a rule says: contact adx_identity_passwordhash, adx_identity_logonenabled, sprk_externalinvitecodehash, sprk_externalinvitedemailhash, sprk_externalinvitedtenantid, sprk_externalinvitedon, sprk_externalobjectid, sprk_externaltenantid, sprk_identityplane, sprk_identitycollision* (prefix), sprk_standinggrant, sprk_accesspermissiongrant, sprk_externalaccessremovedon; sprk_issecure and sprk_accessinheritance on every table; systemuser sprk_hometenantid / sprk_homeobjectid. A rule naming one as its source falls back to the masked read (create/send) or the as-caller read (push), and on Repair keeps today's not-copied rule, with a warning naming the target. One source of truth: a pinned constant in one place (no field-security profile in the repo names these sets) plus an ArchTest that fails when a column in the repo solution XML that is field-secured (IsSecured=1) on contact, systemuser or any table carrying sprk_issecure is neither on the deny-list nor in an explicit allowed list. Must-fire on at least adx_identity_passwordhash and sprk_issecure.
      C4. The app-only read reads only the mapped source columns of that ONE parent row ($select / ColumnSet of exactly those columns), never the whole row or another record.
      C5. Unchanged, each keeps its existing must-fire test: the mapped filing lookup's AppendTo refusal; invariant and access-conferring targets (`IsCopyInvariantColumn`); `MappingSourceCopyGate` (secure-source owner rule); the final whole-row check; adapter defaults; Repair's forward-only, fill-only, owner and lease rules.
      C6. Unit/seam/contract must-fire and must-not-fire tests for every condition, plus a mutation run on each new condition (record which tests fail). No live dev test (owner).
      C7. Log at Information the rule id and the source and target column names (never the value) whenever a secured or caller-unreadable column is copied past the mask, so an audit can find it.
    </uac-r2-conditions>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.Mapping.cs (step 3 mask + 065's `fromFilingRecord`)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/MappingSourceCallerMask.cs (an explicit filing-parent bypass that still enforces C1, C3, C4; keep the class the single gate the ArchTest requires)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/SendTimeFieldMapping.cs (~153)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/FieldMappings/FieldMappingEndpoints.cs (~640–700, `RetrieveSourceRecordValuesAsCallerAsync` ~1058; `filedUnderTheSource`)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.Repair.cs (~1119, ~1267, ~1370–1400, ~1947)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/FieldSecuredSourceRule.cs (home for the C3 deny-list constant, or a sibling file in the same folder)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/MappingSourceCallerMaskGuardTests.cs, tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/FieldSecuredSourceRuleGuardTests.cs (+ the C3 classification guard)</file>
      <file role="modify">existing seam/contract tests for create mapping, send-time mapping, push field-secured source, Repair</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/architecture/SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md, docs/guides/FIELD-MAPPING-ADMIN-GUIDE.md, docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file role="do-not-touch">projects/**/notes and CLAUDE.md (main session), anything under .claude/, CallerWriteAuthorization.cs, and the UAC-r2 do-not-edit files in current-task.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint>Lift applies only when the mapping source is the row's filing parent by table AND id (create: `SourceIsCallersFilingRecordAsync`; push: Filing edge; send: the filing parent; Repair: the row's filing parent). Every other source is byte-for-byte today's behaviour.</constraint>
    <constraint>C1–C7 above are binding.</constraint>
    <constraint>No new endpoint, service, DI registration, package or Dataverse column. Static helpers per ADR-010.</constraint>
    <constraint>Tests go in existing test files or tests/unit/domain/**; never new files under tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/. Never run Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests unfiltered.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Create from the filing parent: a field-secured column the caller cannot read is copied; a log line names rule, source and target (no value).</criterion>
    <criterion>Send from the filing parent: same.</criterion>
    <criterion>Push on a Filing edge: same; through a non-Filing lookup: not copied, warning, counted skipped (065 behaviour).</criterion>
    <criterion>Repair: a field-secured column of the filing parent is copied (fill-only, forward-only unchanged).</criterion>
    <criterion>C1: caller without Read on the parent → no app-only read, nothing copied, same answer as an unknown id (create, send, push).</criterion>
    <criterion>C2: explicit non-filing source (and same id, other table) → mask and Split drop as today (create, send).</criterion>
    <criterion>C3: a rule sourcing adx_identity_passwordhash or sprk_issecure is not copied past the mask on any surface, with a warning naming the target; the classification ArchTest has must-fire and must-not-fire controls.</criterion>
    <criterion>C4: the app read's column set equals the mapped source columns of the one row (test asserts the request).</criterion>
    <criterion>C5 tests still pass; mutation of each new condition fails at least one test.</criterion>
    <criterion>`dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` 0 warnings; filtered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests green; Spaarke.ArchTests green (without --no-build).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <outputs>
    <output>Code, tests and docs above; notes/task-067-notes.md (main session writes it from the agent's report).</output>
  </outputs>
</task>
